From: Producdevity
Subject: [PATCH] sched: reset RT watchdog on blocked wake across class changes

KGSL temporarily promotes its submitting caller to FIFO and restores its prior
class before returning. A caller restored to CFS can then block and wake without
passing through enqueue_task_rt, retaining watchdog ticks across real sleeps.

Move the existing ENQUEUE_WAKEUP timeout reset to common blocked-task activation.
Keep policy changes, light wakes, runnable migration, preemption and yield from
resetting the budget. Leave watchdog limits, stamp and tick accounting intact.

--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -1707,6 +1707,10 @@
 
 static inline void ttwu_activate(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *p, int en_flags)
 {
+	/* A driver can restore a boosted caller to CFS before it blocks. */
+	if (en_flags & ENQUEUE_WAKEUP)
+		p->rt.timeout = 0;
+
 	activate_task(rq, p, en_flags);
 	p->on_rq = TASK_ON_RQ_QUEUED;
 
--- a/kernel/sched/rt.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/rt.c
@@ -1405,9 +1405,6 @@
 
 	schedtune_enqueue_task(p, cpu_of(rq));
 
-	if (flags & ENQUEUE_WAKEUP)
-		rt_se->timeout = 0;
-
 	enqueue_rt_entity(rt_se, flags);
 	walt_inc_cumulative_runnable_avg(rq, p);
 
